Hana (CS): FYI incoming from InfraEdge onboarding — their SDK init is getting lots of 429s when they spin up many workers in parallel. attaching a short log excerpt.
InfraEdge Team: quick log: 'preflight 429 rate_limited; route=/v1/preflight; region=eu-west-1' — using browser-sdk v0.9.3, ~50 concurrent tabs during warmup.
Leo (Solutions): Thanks. Are they creating ephemeral preflight tokens per tab/worker? or reusing a long-lived token?
InfraEdge Team: ephemeral per worker — each worker calls /auth/ephemeral then /v1/preflight. snippet: ```js
for (let i=0;i<50;i++){
  spawnWorker(() => {
    const t = await getEphemeral();
    sdk.init({ token: t }).preflight();
  })
}
```
Leo (Solutions): That will cause a thundering-herd on the preflight path. Two quick asks: (1) can you confirm header X-Client-Region and X-SDK-Version? (2) do you have any client-side splay/jitter?
Megan (OnboardEng): Agreed — this matches a preflight-coalescing gap. Recommend enabling client coalescing (preflight-coalesce=true) + jittered splay on startup. Also moderate parallelism during initial warmup (batch in groups of 5-10).
Paul (SRE): Also double-check API key scopes — if they're using a restricted service key it can route through a different rate-limiter. Paste a recent request trace (headers ok to redact body).
InfraEdge Team: quick test: enabled coalescing + jitter 200-800ms, left parallelism at 50; result: 12/50 preflight attempts returned 429. headers attached (X-SDK-Version: 0.9.3, X-Client-Region: eu-west-1).
Leo (Solutions): Nice progress. Next try: increase ephemeral token reuse window (don't request a new ephemeral for every worker). For example reuse for 15-30s, and set preflight debounce to 500ms. Also use exponential backoff with full jitter for retries. Example pseudocode:
```js
// reuseToken window = 20000ms
let sharedToken = null;
function getWarmupToken(){
  if (sharedToken && Date.now() - sharedToken.ts < 20000) return sharedToken.val;
  sharedToken = { val: fetchEphemeral(), ts: Date.now() };
  return sharedToken.val;
}
// retry: base=200ms, cap=5s, jitter=random(0, base*2^attempt)
```
InfraEdge Team: switched token reuse -> 20s and debounce 500ms, retried 50 parallel, result: 0/50 429s in our staging run. Running a 30m soak now. Huge improvement.
Hana (CS): Amazing — please add exact steps and the code snippets to the onboarding notes so future customers hit this out of the box. I'll flag a docs follow-up and a playbook entry for rate-window defaults.
Megan (OnboardEng): Will do. I'll create a short troubleshooting checklist: 'Symptoms -> Cause -> Quick fixes (coalesce, reuse window, debounce, retry backoff)'. :white_check_mark:
deploy-bot: Branch created: "cs/onboard/infraedge-rate-warmup" by Megan to add playbook and quickstart defaults.
Hana (CS): Thanks team — I'll update the customer and monitor renewal health during initial traffic ramp.
